    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is headlined by **Jose Caballero** (80.26) and **Corbin Carroll** (78.36), both of whom benefit significantly from favorable matchups against left-handed starters. **Jose Caballero** is our primary target today, as he draws the optimal platoon advantage against Corbin, providing a massive +13% boost to his efficiency score. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** continues to be a focal point; despite a slight platoon penalty against Abbott, his elite speed profile and #2 lineup positioning make him an essential anchor in our pursuit of stolen bases. **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71) and **Josh Naylor** (72.21) also offer high-floor production against Sugano and Poulin, respectively, capitalizing on high-xERA matchups that favor our power-hitting core.\n\nIn terms of bench management, **Kyle Karros** (54.01) presents the most interesting case, barely missing the final lineup cut. While he offers a decent platoon edge against Springs, his lower base projection ultimately lost out to the situational upside of **Alex Freeland** (49.51) and **Dalton Rushing** (47.12) in spots where wind and opposing delivery styles offer better stolen base opportunities. We are carefully monitoring **Austin Riley** (52.68); while his score remains marginal, we are banking on his defensive utility and a modest boost from a high-SB-conceding opposing catcher, though the matchup against Peralta remains a potential points trap. As always, we are keeping a close eye on the health status of **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story** while they remain on the IL, but with **Brice Turang** and **Seiya Suzuki** also out of today's starting nines, our flexibility remains restricted for this slate.",
